---
/* L54 - the same label, a different action. One writer: the figures workstream C. */
---

<figure class="fig">
  <div class="fig__frame">
    <img
      class="fig__picture"
      src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}illustrations/L54.jpg`}
      alt="A line drawing of two close dots either side of a dashed threshold line, with a filled box marked acts under one and an empty box marked does not act under the other."
    />
    <svg
      class="fig__svg"
      viewBox="0 0 640 340"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="L54-fig-title L54-fig-desc"
    >
      <title id="L54-fig-title">Two models either side of a threshold</title>
      <desc id="L54-fig-desc">
        A horizontal scale runs from 0.50 to 0.70. A dashed prussian vertical line marks a threshold at 0.6. Two dots sit close to that line, one just above it labelled A 0.62 and one just below labelled B 0.58. Under the higher dot is a tinted box labelled acts, and under the lower dot an empty dashed box labelled does not act. The threshold draws itself, then the dots and the acted-on box pulse.
      </desc>
      <line x1="120" y1="120" x2="560" y2="120" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="140" y1="112" x2="140" y2="128" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="330" y1="112" x2="330" y2="128" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="520" y1="112" x2="520" y2="128" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="130" y="146" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">0.50</text>
      <text x="318" y="146" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">0.60</text>
      <text x="508" y="146" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">0.70</text>

      <path class="m-draw" style="--m-length: 110; --m-duration: 0.9s;" d="M 330 196 L 330 80" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="5 4" />
      <text x="336" y="74" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-prussian)">threshold 0.6</text>

      <circle class="m-pulse" style="--m-duration: 1.1s; --m-delay: 0.5s;" cx="368" cy="120" r="6" fill="var(--color-ink)" />
      <text x="344" y="106" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">A 0.62</text>
      <circle class="m-pulse" style="--m-duration: 1.1s; --m-delay: 0.5s;" cx="292" cy="120" r="6" fill="var(--color-ink)" />
      <text x="268" y="106" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">B 0.58</text>

      <rect class="m-pulse" style="--m-duration: 1.1s; --m-delay: 0.9s;" x="330" y="176" width="96" height="40" fill="var(--color-prussian-tint)" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text class="m-pulse" style="--m-duration: 1.1s; --m-delay: 0.9s;" x="344" y="201" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-prussian)">acts</text>

      <rect x="240" y="176" width="90" height="40" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="4 3" />
      <text x="250" y="201" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">does not act</text>

      <text x="40" y="258" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">the label is the same; what the system does with it is not</text>
      <text x="40" y="274" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">a threshold sits in the middle of two models' outputs all the time,</text>
      <text x="40" y="290" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">so a small gap can flip a decision</text>

    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="fig__caption">
    <span class="edge-code">figure L54</span>
    <span class="fig__caption-text">A threshold sits between two models' outputs, so a gap of a few hundredths is enough to flip whether the system acts at all.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  /* scoped to this figure */
  .fig__svg {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
</style>
